# Knowledge maintainers own the knowledge gate: its verifier bundle, workflows,
# signing key and this file, plus the knowledge tooling and the non-governed
# knowledge paths. With the ruleset's "require review from Code Owners" and
# "dismiss stale approvals", a change here cannot land without a maintainer
# approving its current head (doc/features/knowledge-service.md).
#
# Governed knowledge pages (knowledge/repos/**, knowledge/general/**) have NO
# code owner on purpose: they merge through the kb-gate signed verdict. A
# human-approved verdict must be approved by an owner of /.github/kb-gate/.
#
# @tzhouam is the only maintainer. GitHub does not let an author approve their
# own PR, so the human-approved path covers PRs opened by others; the owner's
# own changes here go through the owner's bypass of the code-owner ruleset
# (see doc/features/knowledge-service.md), never through kb-gate's.

/.github/                 @tzhouam
/knowledge/tools/         @tzhouam
/knowledge/skills/        @tzhouam
